From f5573e38f4f51bdb660f7ec55caf20f836c8b50d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:28:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build on SirisAI's hub contract: inbox, home controls,
 engineering for SirisAI (ADR 110)

- Brief and search come from SirisAI's /siris/hub/v1 in one call each,
  falling back to the old per-tool path on a 404. SirisAI's contract
  examples are copied into the backend tests and drive them (this caught
  a brief printing "70.0% chance of rain").
- Inbox: SirisAI's attention feed (alerts, approvals, suggestions,
  reviews) merged with apps that are down, APD PM overdue tasks and the
  Archive review queue. Live over SSE, with server-side dismissals.
- Home: protocols with preview, confirm and undo; cameras with "What's
  there?"; car, power and parcels. Guest mode hides personal widgets.
- SirisAI's service key opens only read/compute routes. Calculators run
  server-side, with 50 parity cases shared by both test suites.
- SirisHydro synthesis goes through SirisAI's model router.
- Sheets render in a portal, so one opened from a glass card covers the
  page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
